  "disposition": "EXACT_DECLARATIVE_ARRAY_MAP_SYSTEMS_AND_COMPLETE_REFINEMENT_EQUATIONS_SPLIT_UNCOMPILED",
  "conceptual_split_decision": "Separate both complete transition/observation system definitions from the full refinement and its three exact consequences. Preserve every original m/n/f/matrix/specification parameter,all fields and proof terms. Same-source system companion adds no new historical provider or narrowed record.",
  "premise_review": [
    "All2539B original and4146B organized bytes read separately. mapSpecSystem Input=Bool→Bool,State=BitMatrix m n,Resolution=PUnit,Observation=matrix,step=BitMatrix.map and identity observe. mapImplSystem instead uses full ArrayBacked state,mapInPlace and toMatrix observation.",
    "mapRefinement copies all8 original fields exactly:ValidTrue,abstracttoMatrix,mapInputid,mapResolutionid,mapObservationidentity,valid_steptrivial,step_sound exact matrix.mapInPlace_spec f,observe_sound rfl. No DAF.Refinement field or validity premise is dropped.",
    "Both simp theorem attributes retained. mapRefinement_abstract is full arbitrary matrix/rfl; mapRefinement_step_sound keeps full arbitrary f/matrix and exact stored step_sound invocation with trivial validity proof. refines_iff_abstract_eq keeps full matrix/specification and Iff.rfl.",
    "Full12196B ArrayBasic defines ArrayBacked with data:ArrayBool and actual size_eq:data.size=m*n. Its pure logical mapInPlace preserves that invariant and exact mapInPlace_spec proves commutation through toMatrix. The source explicitly distinguishes that logical definition from runtime destructive reuse; no runtime primitive is executed or performance theorem claimed.",
    "Full4028B DAF.Refinement and9553B DAF.System providers read. Refinement soundness is observational,not equality of raw array structure/proof fields,and does not require every implementation value to be a canonical encoding. m/n may be0 and all original types remain exact.",
    "Original DAF.Refinement/BitMatrix.Core.Basic imports remain unchanged. No old/new type alias or provider substitution; only the two complete same-source system definitions are newly imported. Original doc notice explicitly excluding raw-structure/proof-field identification is copied whole into both modules."
  ],
